## Build

This repository uses GNU Make and is configured for WinOS builds only.

The default build works with:

- `clang` / `clang++`
- `gcc` / `g++`
- `cl` (MSVC)
- some Borland/Embarcadero toolchains supported by the shared Makefile

Common commands:

```powershell
make help
make
make build
make rebuild
make clean
make realclean
```

On this checkout, `make help` reports the default output path as:

```text
#build/win.release.(clang@21.1)-x64/bin/console-gui-shim.exe
```

The build tree already contains example outputs for `cl`, `clang`, and `gcc` configurations under [`#build`](#build).

## Configuration Notes

Useful Make variables include:

- `CC` to select the compiler
- `ARCH=32` or `ARCH=64` to pick the target architecture
- `DEBUG=true` to build without release optimizations
- `STATIC=true|false` to control static linking
- `VERBOSE=true` for more build output

Examples:

```powershell
make CC=clang ARCH=64
make CC=gcc ARCH=64 DEBUG=true
make CC=cl ARCH=32
```

## Tests

There is a Catch2-style test file at [`test/test.cpp`](test/test.cpp), and the Makefile exposes `make tests` / `make test`.

At the moment, tests are not buildable as-is in this repository state:

- `test/test.cpp` includes `<catch2/catch_test_macros.hpp>`
- the expected Catch2 headers are not available on the compiler include path during `make tests`
- `make tests` currently fails with a missing-header error

So the test target should be treated as scaffolded rather than working out of the box.

## Implementation Notes

Some behavior worth knowing before reusing or modifying the shim:

- It uses Win32 APIs directly: `CreatePipe`, `CreateProcessW`, `ReadFile`, `WriteFile`, and `CreateThread`.
- It preserves the original command line via `GetCommandLineW()` instead of reconstructing arguments manually.
- It assumes the real target executable has the same basename and lives in the same directory.
- It waits for the stdout echo thread to finish before exiting.

